cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "torChannel: GPU-accelerated DNS of turbulent channel flow in PyTorch"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cavallazzi
    given-names: Giorgio
repository-code: "https://github.com/gmcavallazzi/torChannel"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  A single-GPU direct numerical simulation code for incompressible turbulent
  channel flow, implemented in Python/PyTorch. Second-order staggered finite
  volumes, IMEX time integration with implicit wall-normal diffusion, and an
  FFT-based pressure projection. Includes an RKPM immersed-boundary method for
  rigid filamentous canopies.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - direct numerical simulation
  - turbulence
  - channel flow
  - immersed boundary method
  - PyTorch
  - GPU

